[s0l0!-header][h1]Welcome to C++[/h1][/s0l0!-header]

A C++ program is a collection of [b]commands or statements[/b].

Below is a simple program template.[code format="cpp" ]#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main()
{

  return 0;
}[/code]
You will learn what each of the statements does in the upcoming lessons.
For now, remember that the entry point of every C++ program is the [b]main() [/b]function, irrespective of what the program does.
[note][b]Curly brackets[/b] { } indicate the beginning and end of a function, which can also be called the [b]function's body[/b]. The information inside the brackets indicates what the function does when executed.[/note]

